        <headline>Blowing Dust Advisory issued September 25 at 6:40PM PDT until September 25 at 7:00PM PDT by NWS Spokane WA</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Southwest winds around 20 to 30 mph with gusts up to 45 mph
expected.

* WHERE...Cheney, Moses Lake, Wilbur, Coulee City, Harrington, La
Crosse, Odessa, Oakesdale, Ritzville, Uniontown, Downtown Spokane,
Rosalia, Pullman, Tekoa, Grand Coulee, Ephrata, Davenport, Colfax,
Spokane Valley, Airway Heights, Fairfield, Creston, Quincy,
Rockford, and Othello.

* WHEN...Until 9 PM PDT this evening.

* IMPACTS...Gusty winds will blow around unsecured objects. Tree
limbs could be blown down and a few power outages may result.
</description>
        <instruction>Winds this strong can make driving difficult, especially for high
profile vehicles. Use extra caution.</instruction>
